omx-plugins (0.19.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * omx-delay syncs to the host's tempo: sync, division, mode and duck are
    appended, defaulting to free, 1/4, digital and no duck, so sessions and
    presets sound as before. A CLAP host hands the tempo in the transport, an
    LV2 host as time:Position on the control port; with none, a synced delay
    keeps its Time control (#311).
  * omx-strip's EQ has up to 32 bands, chosen by a Bands control (default 4).
    The existing ids and ports do not move; a band's controls are shown, and
    the CLAP remote-control pages follow, while Bands reaches it (#312, #317,
    #318).
  * New plugins: omx-doubler, omx-tone and omx-ducker, each with CLAP and LV2
    faces and factory presets, over omx-dsp's doubler, tone and comp faces.
  * omx-glue gains Detector Topology, feedforward by default, read from
    comp's declaration; the ssl-bus-glue preset runs the feedback detector,
    and VCA Bus 4:1 is new (#310). omx-comp gains the ducker preset (#309).
  * Readouts on both faces: each meter is an LV2 output control port as well
    as a clap.meters/1 meter, and every descriptor lists its meters, so a host
    can show the dynamic EQ's band gains and the multiband's gain reductions.
    The limiter's reported look-ahead is held to an impulse at every rate
    (#313).
  * The host's bypass keeps one CLAP id, 0x7FFF0000, in every plugin, and
    LV2 enabled and latency are ports 0 and 1, so appending a parameter no
    longer moves them. Sessions and presets go by symbol and are unaffected;
    automation stored on the bypass by id must be bound again (#315).
  * A quiet block still skips the resolve with a tempo: a tempo that moved
    resolves.
  * The MOD GUI film strips are rendered by omx-panel at build time; none is
    committed.
  * The packages install their licence and a short README and no other
    markdown; their descriptions point to openmixer.org (#314).
  * Built on omx-dsp 0.30.0, omx-contract 3.9.0 and omx-panel 0.10.0; those
    are the build floors.
  * Every dependency on a library of ours states a floor and a ceiling in
    debian/control, the spec and omxplugins.pc: omx-dsp >= 0.30.0 and < 0.31,
    omx-contract >= 3.9.0 and < 4, omx-clap-core >= 0.24.0 and < 0.31,
    plugin-hostd >= 0.15.2 and < 0.20, omx-panel >= 0.10.0 and < 0.11,
    plugin-qualify >= 0.9.0 and < 0.20.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

omx-plugins (0.18.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Each plugin runs in place where it is proven to: a host that hands an
    output the buffer of its input (CLAP's in_place_pair, an LV2 host that
    connects both ports to one buffer) gets the same result as with two
    buffers, held by a test per plugin.
  * A quiet block skips the resolve: when no parameter moved since the last
    block, the plugin runs on the coefficients it holds.
  * The CLAP face reads its dirty flag with acquire, against the main
    thread's release store.
  * Built on omx-dsp 0.29.0's fast maths (libmvec where the toolchain has
    it); the build floor is omx-dsp 0.29.0.
  * The CLAP plugins no longer carry the parameter-contract migration members,
    which no plugin ever filled (zero steps everywhere); a host older than omx-
    clap-host 0.23.0 read past the shorter table, so the package declares the
    conflict (#184).

