omx-plugins (0.14.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Our own plugins' pins are known at build time, so they ship with the
    package instead of being recorded by plugin-hostd on first use
    (plugin-hostd issue #42, pins.d): plugin-qualify --pins runs over the
    plugins the build just installed and the result is packaged as
    /usr/share/plugin-hostd/pins.d/omx-plugins.pins, replaced with the
    binaries in the same transaction and removed with the package
    (tools/gen-pins.sh).
  * The package recommends plugin-hostd (>= 0.5.0), the first release that
    reads pins.d: a floor only, no ceiling.
  * dh_auto_install holds the shipped pins to the shipped binaries' own
    hashes: a plugin's binary changed after its pin was written goes red
    (tools/pins-check.sh).
  * The shipped pin is measured after the package is stripped, so it names the
    bytes the package ships: dh_strip (DEB) and the buildroot's strip (RPM) run
    before make install-pins.
  * omx-plugins-test (RPM and DEB) carries the test instruments, a sine voice,
    a note echo and a transport probe, in /usr/libexec/omx-plugins/test,
    outside every CLAP search path; make install-test installs them, make
    install never does. tools/package-lists-check.sh (make package-lists, in
    make test) refuses a built plugin that no package lists.
  * CI runs clap-validator on every built CLAP plugin (tools/clap-validate.sh)
    and keeps the JSON reports; its state-* tests are required
    (tools/clap-validate-required.mjs), the others are reported.
  * Every plugin's CLAP state round trips exactly: a loaded state asks the host
    to rescan the values, the state carries the host's bypass (older states
    still load), a state that names no parameter is refused and a plugin's
    worst-case state fits the loader. clap-probe state, in every plugin's make
    test, checks it.
  * The factory presets, the JSON files in presets/, are offered in every host:
    CLAP preset-discovery (clap.preset-discovery-factory, files in
    /usr/share/omx/presets/<clap id>/) and clap.preset-load, which applies a
    preset's parameters and asks the host to rescan the values, and a
    presets.ttl in each LV2 bundle with one pset:Preset per file. make test
    lists and loads them through CLAP discovery, preset-load and lilv
    (FreeMixer/omx-plugins issue #214).
  * omx-eq8, omx-eq16, omx-eq32 and omx-strip install their descriptors too:
    tools/gen.mjs renders the descriptor of a base of variants and of a chain,
    so the contract directory holds all nineteen and MANIFEST.json lists them;
    their CLAP faces state the parameter modules and their LV2 faces the
    designations, as every described plugin's do
    (tools/test/contract-dir-check.sh requires the four).
  * The round-trip ledger records the seven EQ frequency ports that are authored
    stepped and scan back as log,
    against plugin-hostd issue #147.
  * Every plugin declares its resource hints (omx-contract 3.1.0):
    threads-spawned 0, streams-from-disk false and opens-sockets false,
    served by the CLAP face as org.openmixer.resource-hints.draft/0 and
    stated by the LV2 face as omxres: properties, both from the one
    declaration. The footprints and the activate time stay undeclared until
    a measurement backs them. Builds against omx-contract >= 3.1.0.
  * The Zynthian tarball is repacked from the trixie arm64 DEBs, for ZynthianOS
    Vangelis (Debian trixie); Oram (bookworm) gets no upstream updates. The
    bundle check refuses a glibc symbol above trixie's 2.41 and a library a
    bare trixie lacks (tools/zynthian-bundle.sh, FreeMixer/omx-plugins issue
    #225).

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000

